  "lineage": "Japanese nagauta (\"long song\") sung-and-shamisen narrative tradition serving as the principal musical accompaniment for Kabuki theatre dance-and-action sequences. Codified in mid-Edo period eighteenth century, with the canonical compositional lineages tracing to Kineya Kangoro and Kineya Saburousuke. Performance configuration: a row of male singers seated upstage on a raised platform (typically four-to-eight singers), with a parallel row of shamisen players, plus hayashi percussion ensemble (drums, flutes) on stage-right. Repertoire spans dance-piece accompaniment, dramatic-scene underscore, and standalone concert pieces (the gozen-engaku \"music for the lord\" reception genre). Kineya guild lineages maintain hereditary transmission.",
